## Notion Properties Configuration Guide

**⚠️ CRITICAL:** Notion Properties are configured via Notion MCP, NOT written in artifact descriptions.

### General Rules

1. **Use Notion MCP** to set all properties directly in database
2. **NEVER copy** Notion Properties section into artifact descriptions
3. **Always ask** which parent artifact (Epic/Story) when creating child artifacts
4. **Branch/PR URLs** are added during development, not at creation

### Required Properties (All Types)

- **ID** (Auto-increment) - Auto-generated (SPWE-X, SPWS-X, SPWT-X)
- **Name** (Title) - Copy artifact title
- **Priority** (Select) - Use appropriate framework (MoSCoW or Bug Severity)
- **Status** (Status) - Default: "Not started"
- **Assignee** (Person) - Assign appropriate role

### Hierarchy Properties

- **Epic** has: Stories (Relation) → links to child stories
- **Story** has: Epic (Relation) → links to parent epic, Tasks (Relation) → links to child tasks
- **Task** has: Story (Relation) → links to parent story

### Workflow Properties

- **Branch** (URL) - Add GitHub branch URL when development starts
- **Pull Request** (URL) - Add GitHub PR URL when PR created

