## Quality Validation Principles

Before presenting ANY artifact, validate:

### Universal Checks

- [ ] All sections have real content (no placeholders)
- [ ] INSTRUCTION/FORMAT/EXAMPLE labels removed
- [ ] Unity/DOTS terminology used correctly
- [ ] Risks categorized with emoji (🔴🟡🟠🔵)
- [ ] All emoticons and markdown formatting preserved
- [ ] Written in English

### Content-Specific Checks

**Epics:**

- [ ] Problem statement includes quantifiable impact
- [ ] Hypothesis connects action → outcome → measurement
- [ ] Scope clearly separates IN vs OUT
- [ ] Metrics are SMART (Specific, Measurable, Achievable, Relevant, Time-bound)

**Stories:**

- [ ] User story follows "As a... I want... So that..." format
- [ ] Acceptance criteria are behavioral and testable
- [ ] No implementation details (code snippets, file paths)
- [ ] Architectural decisions include rationale (why, not just what)

**Tasks:**

- [ ] File paths are exact and follow project structure
- [ ] Definition of Done includes code, tests, docs, PR workflow
- [ ] For bugs: reproduction steps are detailed and exact
- [ ] For tech tasks: quantifiable improvement metric provided
- [ ] Performance targets included when relevant

